Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables & columns for the task  
(only columns that matter for ordering and for computing the distance between two consecutive cities):

• geolocation_state: will be the 1st sort key, keeps records grouped by state  
• geolocation_city: 2nd sort key, keeps cities ordered alphabetically inside each state  
• geolocation_zip_code_prefix: 3rd sort key, helps making the ordering unique inside every city  
• geolocation_lat: latitude ‒ used to compute the distance gap with the previous row  
• geolocation_lng: longitude ‒ idem  
Optional filters / conditions that might be useful  
• geolocation_lat IS NOT NULL AND geolocation_lng IS NOT NULL – ignore rows without coordinates  
• You may also want one row per city (e.g. MIN lat/lng for the city) but the question explicitly says to keep the complete ordering, so all rows can stay.  

Below are ten exploratory → increasingly‑complex SQLite queries (each limited to 20 rows) that one would issue while working toward the final answer.  
Every query is wrapped in a code‑block and preceded by a short description comment.

```sql
-- 1. List every distinct state (quick glance at data coverage)
SELECT DISTINCT "geolocation_state"
FROM "olist_geolocation"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. First 20 (state, city) pairs alphabetically
SELECT DISTINCT "geolocation_state",
       "geolocation_city"
FROM   "olist_geolocation"
ORDER  BY "geolocation_state",
          "geolocation_city"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. How many coordinates do we have per state? (sample 20)
SELECT "geolocation_state",
       COUNT(*) AS "n_rows"
FROM   "olist_geolocation"
GROUP  BY "geolocation_state"
ORDER  BY "n_rows" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Check whether any coordinates are NULL
SELECT SUM(CASE WHEN "geolocation_lat" IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "null_lat",
       SUM(CASE WHEN "geolocation_lng" IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "null_lng"
FROM   "olist_geolocation";
```

```sql
-- 5. Preview the ordering required by the problem
SELECT "geolocation_state",
       "geolocation_city",
       "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
       "geolocation_lat",
       "geolocation_lng"
FROM   "olist_geolocation"
ORDER  BY "geolocation_state",
          "geolocation_city",
          "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
          "geolocation_lat",
          "geolocation_lng"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Same ordering, attach the previous row's coordinates via window functions
SELECT "geolocation_state",
       "geolocation_city",
       "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
       "geolocation_lat",
       "geolocation_lng",
       LAG("geolocation_lat") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                             "geolocation_city",
                                             "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                             "geolocation_lat",
                                             "geolocation_lng") AS "prev_lat",
       LAG("geolocation_lng") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                             "geolocation_city",
                                             "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                             "geolocation_lat",
                                             "geolocation_lng") AS "prev_lng"
FROM   "olist_geolocation"
ORDER  BY "geolocation_state",
          "geolocation_city",
          "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
          "geolocation_lat",
          "geolocation_lng"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Compute a simple squared‑Euclidean gap between each row and its predecessor
SELECT "geolocation_state",
       "geolocation_city",
       "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
       "geolocation_lat",
       "geolocation_lng",
       LAG("geolocation_state") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                "geolocation_city",
                                                "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                "geolocation_lat",
                                                "geolocation_lng")  AS "prev_state",
       LAG("geolocation_city")  OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                "geolocation_city",
                                                "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                "geolocation_lat",
                                                "geolocation_lng")  AS "prev_city",
       (( "geolocation_lat" - LAG("geolocation_lat") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                        "geolocation_city",
                                                                        "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                        "geolocation_lat",
                                                                        "geolocation_lng") ) *
        ( "geolocation_lat" - LAG("geolocation_lat") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                        "geolocation_city",
                                                                        "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                        "geolocation_lat",
                                                                        "geolocation_lng") ) +
        ( "geolocation_lng" - LAG("geolocation_lng") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                        "geolocation_city",
                                                                        "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                        "geolocation_lat",
                                                                        "geolocation_lng") ) *
        ( "geolocation_lng" - LAG("geolocation_lng") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                        "geolocation_city",
                                                                        "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                        "geolocation_lat",
                                                                        "geolocation_lng") )
       ) AS "dist2"
FROM   "olist_geolocation"
ORDER  BY "geolocation_state",
          "geolocation_city",
          "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
          "geolocation_lat",
          "geolocation_lng"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Restrict to rows whose predecessor falls in a different city
--    (useful to see city jumps only)
SELECT *
FROM (
      SELECT "geolocation_city",
             LAG("geolocation_city") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                     "geolocation_city",
                                                     "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                     "geolocation_lat",
                                                     "geolocation_lng") AS "prev_city",
             (( "geolocation_lat" - LAG("geolocation_lat") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                              "geolocation_city",
                                                                              "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                              "geolocation_lat",
                                                                              "geolocation_lng") ) *
              ( "geolocation_lat" - LAG("geolocation_lat") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                              "geolocation_city",
                                                                              "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                              "geolocation_lat",
                                                                              "geolocation_lng") ) +
              ( "geolocation_lng" - LAG("geolocation_lng") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                              "geolocation_city",
                                                                              "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                              "geolocation_lat",
                                                                              "geolocation_lng") ) *
              ( "geolocation_lng" - LAG("geolocation_lng") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                              "geolocation_city",
                                                                              "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                              "geolocation_lat",
                                                                              "geolocation_lng") )
             ) AS "dist2"
      FROM   "olist_geolocation"
)
WHERE  "geolocation_city" <> "prev_city"
ORDER  BY "dist2" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Bring the state and both city names for the largest 20 jumps (squared distance)
SELECT "cur_state",
       "cur_city",
       "prev_state",
       "prev_city",
       MAX("dist2") AS "max_dist2"
FROM (
      SELECT "geolocation_state"  AS "cur_state",
             "geolocation_city"   AS "cur_city",
             LAG("geolocation_state") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                     "geolocation_city",
                                                     "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                     "geolocation_lat",
                                                     "geolocation_lng") AS "prev_state",
             LAG("geolocation_city")  OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                     "geolocation_city",
                                                     "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                     "geolocation_lat",
                                                     "geolocation_lng") AS "prev_city",
             (( "geolocation_lat" - LAG("geolocation_lat") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                              "geolocation_city",
                                                                              "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                              "geolocation_lat",
                                                                              "geolocation_lng") ) *
              ( "geolocation_lat" - LAG("geolocation_lat") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                              "geolocation_city",
                                                                              "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                              "geolocation_lat",
                                                                              "geolocation_lng") ) +
              ( "geolocation_lng" - LAG("geolocation_lng") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                              "geolocation_city",
                                                                              "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                              "geolocation_lat",
                                                                              "geolocation_lng") ) *
              ( "geolocation_lng" - LAG("geolocation_lng") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                              "geolocation_city",
                                                                              "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                              "geolocation_lat",
                                                                              "geolocation_lng") )
             ) AS "dist2"
      FROM   "olist_geolocation"
      WHERE  "geolocation_lat" IS NOT NULL
        AND  "geolocation_lng" IS NOT NULL
)
GROUP BY "cur_state", "cur_city", "prev_state", "prev_city"
ORDER  BY "max_dist2" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final answer: the single pair of consecutive cities with the greatest gap
SELECT "cur_state",
       "cur_city",
       "prev_state",
       "prev_city",
       "dist2"                              AS "squared_distance_gap",
       SQRT("dist2")                        AS "euclidean_gap_deg"
FROM (
      SELECT "geolocation_state"  AS "cur_state",
             "geolocation_city"   AS "cur_city",
             LAG("geolocation_state") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                     "geolocation_city",
                                                     "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                     "geolocation_lat",
                                                     "geolocation_lng") AS "prev_state",
             LAG("geolocation_city")  OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                     "geolocation_city",
                                                     "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                     "geolocation_lat",
                                                     "geolocation_lng") AS "prev_city",
             (( "geolocation_lat" - LAG("geolocation_lat") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                              "geolocation_city",
                                                                              "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                              "geolocation_lat",
                                                                              "geolocation_lng") ) *
              ( "geolocation_lat" - LAG("geolocation_lat") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                              "geolocation_city",
                                                                              "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                              "geolocation_lat",
                                                                              "geolocation_lng") ) +
              ( "geolocation_lng" - LAG("geolocation_lng") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                              "geolocation_city",
                                                                              "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                              "geolocation_lat",
                                                                              "geolocation_lng") ) *
              ( "geolocation_lng" - LAG("geolocation_lng") OVER (ORDER BY "geolocation_state",
                                                                              "geolocation_city",
                                                                              "geolocation_zip_code_prefix",
                                                                              "geolocation_lat",
                                                                              "geolocation_lng") )
             ) AS "dist2"
      FROM   "olist_geolocation"
      WHERE  "geolocation_lat" IS NOT NULL
        AND  "geolocation_lng" IS NOT NULL
)
WHERE  "prev_city" IS NOT NULL
ORDER  BY "dist2" DESC
LIMIT 20;  -- LIMIT 20 just to fit the requirement; first row is the answer
```

